We are looking for a Java Backend Engineer to join a global team and contribute to the development of scalable, secure and resilient backend solutions. This role is a great fit for someone with strong hands-on experience in Java, Spring Boot/Quarkus and microservices , combined with practical exposure to cloud technologies and Infrastructure as Code .
 Responsibilities: 
Implement highly scalable, secure, and resilient backend solutions using Java 17+ and Spring Boot; 
Develop, test, and document Java/Kotlin-based software components in accordance with requirements, actively contributing to all stages of the software development lifecycle; 
Maintain high standards of software quality by adhering to good practices and habits, including thorough code reviews and contributing to technical standards; 
Identify and resolve complex technical issues, ensuring system stability and performance; 
Write comprehensive unit tests for robustness, edge cases, and general reliability, and participate in peer-reviews of solution designs and related code; 
Leverage Google Cloud Platform (GCP) services to build, deploy, and manage robust scalable software solutions; 
Collaborate with BAs, QAs, and stakeholders to jointly develop effective solutions; 
Provide support to ensure high-quality releases; 
Thrive in a scaled Agile working environment, collaborating with a global and diverse team; 
 Skills & Experience: 
Deep expertise in Java 17+ and the Spring or Quarkus ecosystem , microservices architecture, docker containers, Kubernetes; 
Good understanding of design patterns, awareness/understanding of SOLID principles; 
Knowledge of Data structures/Collections; 
 Proven experience designing and building scalable backend solutions and RESTful APIs; Java (Spring Framework) or Node.js (Express, Nest.js with TypeScript) 
 Experience with relational and NoSQL databases, including advanced SQL, and schema design; 
 Experience with OAuth2 authorization framework 
Good understating microservices architecture; 
 Good knowledge of Terraform or other equivalent IaC tools (would be a plus) 
 Hands-on relevant experience on cloud; Google Cloud Platform (GCP) (would be a plus) 
 Experience with DevOps, CI/CD, pipelines 
Voracious learner. You’re quick to share tips and tools you’ve picked up and you’re open to learning new things from your co-workers. 
At least one year of relevant experience with any Cloud platform (Azure, AWS, GCP). The experience should be hands-on. Not only just mention. Not only Docker or Kubernetes. 
At least 6 months of using Terraform or any other alternative IaC tool. 
At least 5 years of backend engineering background with the following technologies: 
 > Language: Java/Kotlin 
 > Framework: Spring Boot/Quarkus 
 What do we offer? 
25 holiday days per year.
1066 RON monthly budget in Benefit Online Platform.
Life Insurance cover.
The employees working on bank holidays will be benefitting either of a paid day off in the next 30 days + 100% of the hourly base salary for that specific day OR 200% of the hourly base salary for that specific day.
Reimbursement for eyeglasses – max 1500 RON to be claimed every 3 years.
Childbirth allowance of 7000 RON after 1 year in HCLTech.
Internal trainings and certifications.
 Who are we? 
 We are HCLTech, one of the fastest-growing large tech companies in the world and home to 225,000+ people across 60 countries, supercharging progress through industry-leading capabilities centered around Digital, Engineering and Cloud. The driving force behind that work, our people, are diverse, creative, and passionate, raising the bar for excellence on a regular basis.
